    "q-90676": {
      "dom_id": "step-q90676",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[-4,4],$ find $\\text{E}[X].$",
      "worked_solution": "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-4$ and $b=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{-4+4}{2}=0.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
