    "q-130698": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130698",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[0,100],$ find $\\text{E}[X].$",
      "worked_solution": "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=0$ and $b=100.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{0+100}{2}=50.\n$$",
