    "q-130711": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130711",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[-7,-4],$ find $\\text{Var}[X].$",
      "worked_solution": "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-7$ and $b=-4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(-4-(-7))^{2}}{12}=\\frac{9}{12}=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
