    "q-130726": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130726",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[-10,5],$ find $\\text{SD}[X].$ Round your answer to three decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-10$ and $b=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(5-(-10))^{2}}{12}=\\frac{225}{12}=\\frac{75}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\frac{75}{4}}=\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}≈4.330.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
